"from": "awakens terrified.- Skin dirty, greasy look ing, with yellow blotches here and there, and a partially developed eruption on the forehead and chest. Body always has a filthy smell, even after a bath. Feels particularly well the day before an attack. Sick babies will not sleep day or night, but worry, fret and cry. Although the dark fluid stool is very character istic of Psor., the very offensive odor is much more so. This alone often indicates it in infantile diarrhoea, or in cholera infantum, whatever may be the stool",
